{{!-- duration — the post's reading/watching time, from an internal tag.

     Prints the tag's DESCRIPTION, never its slug. `#duration-1h-5m` carries
     description "1h 5m", so the author writes the display text in Ghost Admin
     and the theme never parses the slug. Parsing would mean the theme owns
     the format, and then `#duration-90m` needs a code change.

     Falls back to Ghost's own {{reading_time}}, which is computed from the
     word count — right for an article, useless for a video, which is exactly
     why the tag exists. --}}
{{~#foreach tags visibility="internal"~}}
    {{~#match slug "~^" "hash-duration-"~}}{{description}}{{~/match~}}
{{~/foreach~}}
